A||N||15||KATIE71858||TRANSMISSION PROBLEMS PLEASE HELP!!||||5||
Z||000000||KATIE71858||10-03-2001||06:40 PM||||OK, I WAS GOING DOWN THE ROAD ONE DAY AND I NOTICED THAT WHEN I PUSHED THE CLUTCH IN ON MY 86'FIERO 2.8, 4SPD. THAT IT WOULD MAKE A TICKING SOUND UNDER THE DASH. A DAY OR TWO LATER WHEN I PUSHED THE CLUTCH IN IT MADE A POPPING NOISE LOUD UNDER THE DASH AND THEN THE CLUTCH WOULD NOT DISENGAGE FULLY. I NOTICED THAT WHEN I PUSHED THE CLUTCH IN AFTER THAT IT WOULD NOT GO ALL THE WAY TO THE FLOOR. WHEN I TOOK THE CAR TO THE REPAIR SHOP I TOLD THE MECHANIC WHAT HAPPEND AND TOLD HIM THAT I THAUGHT THE CLUTCH PEDAL MAY HAVE BENT. HE SAID THAT IT DIDNT FROM LOOKING AT IT. HE THEN SAID THAT IT NEEDED A NEW CLUTCH, PRESSURE PLATE, AND THROUGH OUT BARRING. HE REPLACED THAT THEN HE REPLACED THE CLUTCH MASTER CYLINDER, THE SLAVE CYLINDER AND BRACKET PUT IT ALL BACK TOGETHER AND IT STILL DID THE SAME THING... HE SAYS THAT IT HE DOESNT KNOW WHAT THE PROBLEM IS AND MY CAR IS SITTING OVER THERE FOR TWO WEEKS AND I REALLY NEED SOME HELP DOES ANYONE HAVE ANY SUGGESTIONS???? PLEASE RESPOND ASAP!||||reg||5
Z||000001||PAUL88GT||10-03-2001||07:00 PM||||Is your mechanic experienced on Fieros?  A common problem is the bent clutch pedel.  The original aluminum pedal has be to replaced with new steel one which cost about $30.  I would replace the clutch pedal before doing anything to the transaxle. There have been many bargain Fieros purchased because of this simple problem. Perform a search in the Tech section and let your mechanic read some of them. Either way, sounds like you will have an entirely new clutch system whether you needed it or not.<P>By the way, welcome to the forum and I hope you like attention. You will get plenty of help based on you forum name.<P>You may want to consider bringing your car to Ed Parks of the Fiero Factory near Huntsville, AL.  Ed is a Fiero specialist and is not too far from SC.  <P>[This message has been edited by PAUL88GT (edited 10-03-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by PAUL88GT (edited 10-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||California Kid||10-03-2001||07:37 PM||||There's also a bushing in the clutch pedal itself that may have failed, causing the clicking and snapping noises your heard. From your description before you took it into the shop, it sounds like all you might have needed is the pedal to be replaced or just the bushing in the pedal.||||reg||1
Z||000003||KATIE71858||10-03-2001||07:40 PM||||WHERE CAN I GET A NEW CLUTCH PEDAL AND ALL THE HARDWARE TO REPLACE IT.||||reg||1
Z||000004||PAUL88GT||10-03-2001||10:18 PM||||Clutch pedal:  <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.gmpartsdirect.com</A> <BR>Bushings: try: <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A>  <P>Also, use the search function on the upper right and search on "clutch pedal" and you will find all the answers you need on this subject.||||reg||1
