Z||000009||k2m4||10-05-2001||01:32 PM||||Hey ms Katie...These guys ALL know what they are talking about. I would take thier word on the situation. i havent asked too many questions here on the board cause ive ALWAYS found my answer in the archives and the few times i have asked its been right on the money with thier diagnosisees (sp?) More than likely it is your clutch pedal. <P>Like some one said above print this out and show your mechanic. <P>86 2M4<BR>86 GT||||reg||14
Z||000010||Joe Torma||10-05-2001||02:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KATIE71858:<BR><B>If the pedal is not the problem what else could be the problem??? Im desperate please help!!!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ok, what is happening now?  You've got lots of "new" parts.  <P>Is is still popping? ---Probably the pedal, rod, bushings<P>Does it still not disengage?  ---above, and/or bleed the slave cylander.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||KATIE71858||10-06-2001||08:43 AM||||Ok, the clutch pedal is now new, the mechanic got a clutch from a diffrent company and it did the same thing all over again! Any suggestions? He said that he has called the GM tech line so many times that GM is going to send a tech out there to help him with it... any other suggestions on what might be the problem??||||reg||5
Z||000012||KATIE71858||10-09-2001||09:29 PM||||Could the cluch arm on the tanny be causing this problem?? Please going on 3 weeks in the shop HELP!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000013||TooManyFieros||10-10-2001||08:54 AM||||If the clutch "banjo" rod from the pedal to the master cylinder is upside down, it will cause a poping problem when the pedal is depressed about halfway down. Disconnect it from the pedal and turn it 180 deg. Been there, found that.  Jim||||reg||7
Z||000014||Joe Torma||10-10-2001||09:56 AM||||I had to replace the fork inside the bell housing(presses up against the throwout bearing).  No noise from under the dash, but when worn, the pedal is notchy and doesn't feel right.<P>The mechanic put another clutch in?||||reg||1
Z||000015||stsmithgt||10-10-2001||09:57 AM||||Wow... Sounds like your mechanic was using the ol' "shotgun" technique to try to solve your problem.  That's a commom practice with Fieros so I've found out too.  If everything under the dash turns out to be OK, probably not, I recently experienced a clutch fork failure that had similar symtoms and noises.  If he's not familiar with Fieros, that could be easily overlooked.  I will get pics up with the failed one soon.... (2 cents deposited)||||reg||1
